mal ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1,"offset":1559},"end":{"line":38,"column":44,"offset":1602}}},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transferChecked()","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":44,"offset":1602},"end":{"line":38,"column":63,"offset":1621}}},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":63,"offset":1621},"end":{"line":38,"column":65,"offset":1623}}},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"burnChecked()","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":65,"offset":1623},"end":{"line":38,"column":80,"offset":1638}}},{"type":"text","value":", ... instructions and pass in the ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":80,"offset":1638},"end":{"line":38,"column":115,"offset":1673}}},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PermanentDelegate","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":115,"offset":1673},"end":{"line":38,"column":134,"offset":1692}}},{"type":"text","value":" authority in the ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":134,"offset":1692},"end":{"line":38,"column":152,"offset":1710}}},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authority","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":152,"offset":1710},"end":{"line":38,"column":163,"offset":1721}}},{"type":"text","value":" field.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":163,"offset":1721},"end":{"line":38,"column":170,"offset":1728}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1,"offset":1559},"end":{"line":38,"column":170,"offset":1728}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1,"offset":0},"end":{"line":38,"column":170,"offset":1728}}},"raw":"import { ArticleSection } from \"../../../../components/ArticleSection/ArticleSection\";\r\n\r\n# The Permanent Delegate Extension\r\n\r\nThe `PermanentDelegate` extension is a Mint account extension that allows a permanent delegate for all tokens of the mint that is capable of transferring or burning any token of that mint, from any token account.\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Initializing the Mint Account\" id=\"initializing-the-mint-account\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nTo initialize the `PermanentDelegate` extension on a `Mint` account we can simply use the macro that `Anchor` created for us.\r\n\r\nHere's how to create a mint with the Permanent Delegate extension:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n#[derive(Accounts)]\r\npub struct CreateMint<'info> {\r\n    #[account(mut)]\r\n    pub signer: Signer<'info>,\r\n    #[account(\r\n        init,\r\n        payer = signer,\r\n        mint::decimals = 6,\r\n        mint::authority = signer.key(),\r\n        mint::token_program = token_program\r\n        extensions::permanent_delegate::delegate = signer,\r\n    )]\r\n    pub mint: InterfaceAccount<'info, Mint>,\r\n    pub system_program: Program<'info, System>,\r\n    pub token_program: Interface<'info, TokenInterface>,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Permissioned Actions\" id=\"permissioned-actions\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nUnlike regular delegates which can be revoked, this delegate authority is permanent and immutable. \r\n\r\nThis means that every normal action like `transfer()`, `burn()`, `approve()` and `freeze()` can be executed whenever needed directly by the authority without needing the signature of the actual owner.\r\n\r\nThis means that we can just use the normal `transferChecked()`, `burnChecked()`, ... instructions and pass in the `PermanentDelegate` authority in the `authority` field.","highlightedCode":{"code-0":{"lang":"rust","hast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"pre","properties":{"class":"shiki Kiloshift","style":"background-color:#11141a;color:#f6f6f4","tabindex":"0"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#F6F6F4"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"#[derive("}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"style":"color:#97E1F1;font-style:italic"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accounts"}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","